        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 266.31,
          "end": 269.1,
          "en": "Well then we would simply add posts as a segment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.1,
          "end": 272.58,
          "en": "And important for Firebase, you need to add dot Jason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 272.58,
          "end": 274.62,
          "en": "This simply is a Firebase requirement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 274.62,
          "end": 278.07,
          "en": "It's not an Angular requirement, not a REST API requirement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.07,
          "end": 281.073,
          "en": "Only a requirement by that Firebase REST API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 285.063,
          "en": "This now allows us to send a post request to that URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 286.2,
          "end": 289.05,
          "en": "Now since it's a post request, it doesn't work just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 289.05,
          "end": 289.883,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.883,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "However, a post request also needs a request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 296.94,
          "en": "Now this post method here works such that it takes more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.94,
          "end": 297.9,
          "en": "than one argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 297.9,
          "end": 300.42,
          "en": "It has at least two required arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.42,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "The second argument being the request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 306.45,
          "en": "So we pass one additional argument here and that could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 306.45,
          "end": 307.74,
          "en": "our post data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 307.74,
          "end": 310.71,
          "en": "So the data, we wanna store this data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 310.71,
          "end": 315.24,
          "en": "Now very important, you normally send Jason data when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 315.24,
          "end": 317.28,
          "en": "interacting with a restful API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.28,
          "end": 319.62,
          "en": "And actually that will happen here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 319.62,
          "end": 323.15,
          "en": "But the Angular HTTP client will take our JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.15,
          "end": 327.36,
          "en": "here and automatically convert it to Jason data for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 327.36,
          "end": 330.03,
          "en": "So it will still send Jason data and we'll see this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 330.03,
          "end": 332.22,
          "en": "in a second when we inspect that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 334.14,
          "en": "in the browser developer tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 334.14,
          "end": 336.81,
          "en": "But it will, Angular will transform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 336.81,
          "end": 338.622,
          "en": "this automatically for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 338.622,
          "end": 341.46,
          "en": "Now with this we have a request that should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 341.46,
          "end": 343.35,
          "en": "It has all the core data it needs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 343.35,
          "end": 345.69,
          "en": "the URL and the request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 345.69,
          "end": 348.84000000000003,
          "en": "And for now, we don't need to set any our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
