          "start": 375.392,
          "end": 377.43,
          "en": "You see a bunch of network requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 377.43,
          "end": 379.74,
          "en": "Actually, these are all the files that are downloaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 379.74,
          "end": 382.428,
          "en": "as part of your Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 382.428,
          "end": 384.84,
          "en": "and all the JavaScript files is on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 384.84,
          "end": 385.71,
          "en": "Let's clear that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 385.71,
          "end": 387.824,
          "en": "Let's simply send another post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 387.824,
          "end": 390.18,
          "en": "and we don't see any request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 390.18,
          "end": 393.652,
          "en": "So somehow this request is not being sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 393.652,
          "end": 396.825,
          "en": "and that happens on purpose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 396.825,
          "end": 401.43,
          "en": "Angular heavily uses observables as you already learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 401.43,
          "end": 403.98,
          "en": "And HTTP requests are also managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 403.98,
          "end": 407.46,
          "en": "via observables because they are a perfect scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 407.46,
          "end": 409.56,
          "en": "or use case for observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 409.56,
          "end": 411.96,
          "en": "We can wrap them and we can then subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 411.96,
          "end": 413.1,
          "en": "to them to get informed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 413.1,
          "end": 416.73,
          "en": "about the response and to handle errors and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 416.73,
          "end": 420.12,
          "en": "The thing just is, Angular is smart, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 420.12,
          "end": 422.168,
          "en": "If you're not subscribing to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 422.168,
          "end": 425.325,
          "en": "prepared HTTP request you could save.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 425.325,
          "end": 428.76,
          "en": "So to that observable, that wraps your HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 428.76,
          "end": 431.7,
          "en": "If you're not subscribing to it, then Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 431.7,
          "end": 435.51,
          "en": "and RXJS know that no one's interested in the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 435.51,
          "end": 437.88,
          "en": "and therefore the request doesn't even get sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 437.88,
          "end": 440.25,
          "en": "Because if no one's interested in the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 440.25,
          "end": 442.337,
          "en": "then it won't send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 442.337,
          "end": 446.82,
          "en": "So Post Indeed will return an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 446.82,
          "end": 448.14300000000003,
          "en": "As you can also see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 449.13,
          "end": 451.02,
          "en": "it does not give us the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 451.02,
          "end": 452.90999999999997,
          "en": "or anything like that as a return value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 452.90999999999997,
          "end": 456.15,
          "en": "It gives us an observable that wraps your request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 456.15,
          "end": 457.86,
          "en": "And to get access to the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 457.86,
          "end": 460.53,
          "en": "you have to call subscribe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 460.53,
          "end": 463.49,
          "en": "And this will then be your response data, actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 463.49,
          "end": 466.98,
          "en": "Because Angular, the HTTP client I should say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 466.98,
          "end": 469.65,
          "en": "will do even more than just giving you the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 469.65,
          "end": 472.56,
          "en": "it will automatically extract the data attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 472.56,
          "end": 476.49,
          "en": "to the response, so the response body, and give you that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 476.49,
          "end": 479.34000000000003,
          "en": "Though you also have ways of accessing the full response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 479.34000000000003,
          "end": 481.59,
          "en": "as you'll learn later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 481.59,
          "end": 485.13,
          "en": "So for now, let's simply console lock that response data to",
          "zh": ""
        },
